# Environment configuration for JoustMania
# Copy this file to the git-ignored .env.local (never over the tracked .env,
# which holds the release IMAGE_TAG) and keep it private; ./setup.sh offers this:
#   install -m 600 .env.example .env.local
# Never set IMAGE_TAG in .env.local on the Pi: the pinned checkout decides it
# (UC-060 BR-003).

# ---- Decision-backend API keys (#1244) ----
# Do NOT put API keys in .env: it is TRACKED in git despite .gitignore.
# Export them in your shell, or put them in the git-ignored .env.local and load
# both files (later wins; passing --env-file disables the implicit .env):
#   docker compose --env-file .env --env-file .env.local up -d
# The keys go straight to the agent (no gateway); an empty key keeps that
# backend unavailable, so decisions fall back to rules. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY also
# serves the post-game retro / experiment proposer when
# the inference.backend flag is claude (#1234, #1810).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# DECISION_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# JEV_API_KEY=

# ---- Dashboard host names (UC-005 BR-003, #1450) ----
# Extra host names the operator uses to open the dashboard (comma-separated).
# Always allowed without this: IP literals, localhost, and the Pi's own host
# name and <hostname>.local (compose mounts the host's /etc/hostname). The
# unpair endpoint answers 403 for any other Host (DNS-rebinding guard).
# Default: empty.
# JOUSTMANIA_HOSTNAMES=joustmania.example,stage-pi

# ---- Opt-in compose profiles (UC-060) ----
# Put these in the git-ignored .env.local on the Pi, never in .env.
# The operator pad (UC-015, #2050) starts only with its profile. Set the whole
# comma-separated list in one place (e.g. python-hid,operator-pad): a unit
# drop-in Environment=COMPOSE_PROFILES=... wins over .env.local, and a profile
# missing from the winning list is off (the start script removes its container).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=operator-pad
# GID of the host's input group (owner of /dev/input/event*), host identity
# (C-035, flags.md §15.2). `getent group input` shows it. Default: 996 (stage Pi).
# INPUT_GID=996
